{"step_index":1350,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:59:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:59:35+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:59:36+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:59:35+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:59:36+08:00\nShowing lines 565-600 of 1075\n565: function switchTab(activeBtnId) {\n566:   tabs.forEach(([b, v]) => {\n567:     const on = b === activeBtnId;\n568:     $(b).classList.toggle('active', on);\n569:     $(v).classList.toggle('hide', !on);\n570:   });\n571:   if (activeBtnId !== 'tab-btn-sub') $('sub-status-msg').classList.add('hide');\n572:   syncSubPoller();\n573:   if (activeBtnId === 'tab-btn-sub') refreshSubmissions();\n574: }\n575: tabs.forEach(([b]) => {\n576:   $(b).onclick = () => switchTab(b);\n577: });\n578: \n579: function showDashboard() {\n580:   quizLoadSeq++;\n581:   closeEdge();\n582:   stopSubPoller();\n583:   $('main-nav').classList.add('hide');\n584:   $('opt-btn').classList.add('hide');\n585:   $('view-editor').classList.add('hide');\n586:   $('view-sub').classList.add('hide');\n587:   $('sub-status-msg').classList.add('hide');\n588:   $('dash-msg').classList.add('hide');\n589:   $('view-dash').classList.remove('hide');\n590:   if (!quizCatalog.length) quizCatalog = mergeQuizCatalog([]);\n591:   renderDashboard();\n592:   refreshDashboard();\n593: }\n594: $('tab-btn-dash').onclick = showDashboard;\n595: \n596: function openRenameModal(item) {\n597:   renameTarget = item;\n598:   $('rename-input').value = item.label;\n599:   $('rename-modal').classList.remove('hide');\n600:   if ($('rename-input').focus) $('rename-input').focus();"}
{"step_index":1351,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:59:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:59:35+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:59:41+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:59:35+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:59:41+08:00\nThe search for \"master detail web UI back button vs top nav tab navigation URL history replaceState vanilla JS\" returned the following summary:\nWhen designing a **Master-Detail web UI** with tab navigation using vanilla JavaScript, managing the browser's history correctly is vital[1]. A common UX bug is \"back-button hijacking\"—where clicking through tabs or detail views forces the user to press the back button dozens of times just to leave the page[2].\n\nThe core architectural choice comes down to knowing when to use **`history.pushState()`** versus **`history.replaceState()`**[3].\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Rules: `pushState` vs `replaceState`\n\n*   **`pushState()` (Create a new history entry):** Use this when the user navigates to a **genuinely new context or drill-down** (e.g., clicking a Master item to open the Detail view). The user expects the browser’s Back button to return them to the previous master state[3].\n*   **`replaceState()` (Modify the current history entry):** Use this when switching **tabs, filters, or sub-views *within* the same context** (e.g., switching from the \"Overview\" tab to the \"Settings\" tab inside a Detail view)[3]. This keeps the URL updated for bookmarking/sharing without cluttering the browser's history stack with redundant steps[4][3][1].\n\n---\n\n### 2. Recommended Navigation Flow Pattern\n\n1.  **List to Detail (Master Click):** Use **`pushState`**. \n    *   *Why:* Going from a list of 20 items to inspecting Item A is a structural navigation step. Back should close/leave the detail view.\n2.  **Tab Switching inside Detail:** Use **`replaceState`**.\n    *   *Why:* If a user clicks \"Overview\" $\\rightarrow$ \"Activity\" $\\rightarrow$ \"Settings\" inside Item A's detail page, clicking \"Back\" should take them *back to the Master list*, not cycle backward through Item A's tabs[3].\n\n---\n\n### 3. Vanilla JavaScript Implementation Blueprint\n\nHere \n<truncated 3277 bytes>\n.search);\n  const tab = params.get('tab') || 'overview';\n\n  if (itemId) {\n    renderDetail(itemId, tab);\n  }\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary Checklist for Best UX\n\n| Action Performed by User | History Method to Use | Expected Back Button Behavior |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Master $\\rightarrow$ Detail** | `history.pushState()`[3] | Returns user back to the master list[3]. |\n| **Switching Tabs (Overview $\\leftrightarrow$ Settings)** | `history.replaceState()`[3] | Skips intermediate tabs and returns user directly to the master list[3]. |\n| **Applying Filters / Search Queries** | `history.replaceState()`[3] | Updates URL for link sharing, but pressing back exits the filtered view instead of undoing every keystroke/filter toggle[3][2]. |\n\nSources:\n[1] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFBb_NxOjv6PHXanyjbVDHhJW6WPC0EIk6Ut-fb7t1JY905Ju6u_MIMGzTwoJZI2PF5iC-NH9SQwwqkAUi3Rc3X8u01MPXvTPq82d_YbZ0muQlQD_lEvTyjDISOXg82hkqPf5DrFUIJh1GTracWupQrf6kDxapSXUHUg2leBCghPOX294EMzDElKFSRrv0Pv3FoyBu8CAkTZXKHM7kipb0Z3xbbRR2mfnLy9ch0KrjU5JSegXGTFIc=)\n[2] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHbmZhvK9IK5bl4lFVKlAGVu9wwurNU_JmyVY56LQOO2Zo6swFmM_sS1WT73bq3PbxcVss5-cJ5CIsoeJu_fGEbp-SbpQbWZfzbfuJ4v9jJXWcIcOegdBvvdhYC8QTpoi7HJ7cC17oZ79Y2E839gW0FSQ28CAoQEFQiIX_Jh610JlBCZThJtvGQb7EKGsiIXkwTjQ==)\n[3] [frontend-routing.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG4pJJRKXrX2ZNONYV0ckDl0xkTyTeZYoBWLSySQpzfEJJaCCPmRPHZsp7dLe8eg-AiYCFOwtP4sQSvFu333kRcrTtHGb7cf8JUgOLSQbY0kjq5lBrxg1agazZvMjhkRsxD6tqPQjnjwRWMEPI7qiMHlhiUARfezNlTJMswgVMDmG1BnOlpZQF_Fa6L2e66eVTAJEwlsuNCxJRcR2s6JKv4NaIl0SJTmPc_NPY6sMxfzoTZ__rweNJfnQciTEY=)\n[4] [willschenk.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHhZ5GJTDQ6R6Lgkc0UB4v39plvTzWD17lRjyuygLCTw819LgLcoyyahW63M7NUnix7iaduyhkGnmwzy248Kn6yFuORwO3ZJLWNz8-o6YWigLTkB0kjdDUkO6aPKgnHzZ9wjGgVhvGXUZEPemg=)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
